A||N||10||87GTjoe||sunroof install||||5||
Z||000000||87GTjoe||05-26-2001||07:12 PM||||I was wanting to take the roof section off of a parts car and install it on my 87GT so that I can have a sunroof.How much of a pain will this be? Does the windshield have to be removed in order to do this? Any tips on this would be greatly appreciated.Thanks,Joe||||reg||5
Z||000001||PBJ||05-26-2001||07:48 PM||||Yes the windshield will have to be removed to swap exterior roof sections. Unless you were going to put in an aftermarket sunroof-that would just require cutting on the vehicle, but I don't think aftermarket roofs are or can be as big as the factory ones.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Wolfhound||05-26-2001||09:51 PM||||The windshield will not have to be removed. The black molding around it will.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rodrv6||05-26-2001||09:53 PM||||Ummmm... You don't have to take the windshield out to change the roof.  If you pull out the trim that goes around the windshield and carefully cut around the edge of the glass to separate the sealer from the roof section the window can stay put.  The sections that go down each side of the windshield are very fragile, so a lot of care and patience is needed to avoid breaking the roof.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||1
Z||000004||87GTjoe||05-27-2001||11:43 AM||||Came off in one piece,alot easier than I thought it would be.Hopefully it wont leak.Thanks for the help,Joe||||reg||1
Z||000005||KRMFiero||05-27-2001||01:07 PM||||Hi, im planning to do this swap sometime soon, do you have any tips, what tools you used, what you had to remove that may help me<P>kyle||||reg||1
Z||000006||cadaver||05-27-2001||01:27 PM||||Maybe its olny those british fiero that you need to pull the windshield to get the roof off?<P>Make sure you also get the brackets from under the hood that hold the glass panel when its stowed. And you may need to swap to the smaller windshield washer bottle.||||reg||1
Z||000007||87GTjoe||05-27-2001||03:32 PM||||Just finished bolting everything together.The brackets for stowing the glass under the hood bolted right in and the washer bottle didnt have to move.Anybody have a dark grey headliner they want to sell??||||reg||1
Z||000008||cadaver||05-28-2001||12:02 AM||||Thats funny. When I did mine I had to swap to the smaller bottle. Yours might have the smaller already.<BR>Did you also grab the wind deflector?||||reg||1
Z||000009||87GTjoe||05-28-2001||04:40 AM||||Got that too.The only thing I need now is the bag to put the glass in.||||reg||1
Z||000010||mbramble||05-28-2001||10:39 AM||||KRMFiero, there is a very good "how-to" for doing the sunroof swap at <A HREF="http://www.cyberverse.com/~cyco/fieroparts/tips/sunroof.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cyberverse.com/~cyco/fieroparts/tips/sunroof.htm</A> <P>Mike<BR>||||reg||1
